# Raw data. Naming convention (phase 2):  origen_tema_periodo_version.csv
datos/crudos/*

# ...with two deliberate exceptions, both of which belong in the repo.
#
# 1. The FIFA figures. Transcribed by hand from the annual Global Transfer Report,
#    one row per year and age band, each carrying its edition, figure and page.
#    The PDFs themselves are NOT redistributed: FIFA publishes them under no open
#    licence. These CSVs are our transcription of published facts, and without them
#    the aggregate half of the case could not be rebuilt.
!datos/crudos/fifa_*.csv

# 2. The Transfermarkt snapshot. The upstream dataset is refreshed WEEKLY, so a
#    download three months from now returns different numbers and the case stops
#    reproducing. Ten megabytes is a small price for a result that still holds.
#    (The rule against versioning raw data exists because of size — case 1 was
#    383 MB. This is not that.)
!datos/crudos/transfermarkt_*.csv.gz

# Derived datasets: regenerated by `python notebooks/procesar.py`.
#
# Note the trailing /* instead of /: git does not descend into an excluded directory,
# so `datos/limpios/` followed by `!datos/limpios/.gitkeep` would never re-admit the
# file and the folder would not reach a new repo at all. Ignoring the CONTENT keeps
# the exception reachable.
datos/limpios/*
!datos/limpios/.gitkeep
datos/intermedios/*
!datos/intermedios/.gitkeep

# OS / environment junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
